  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">Output 6.4. Increased capacity of ILO constituents to strengthen legislation, polices and measures to ensure equal opportunities and treatment in the world of work for persons with disabilities and other persons in vulnerable situations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="ES">1. The Ministry of Social Affairs and Labour and the Haitian Industrial Association and workers&#x2019; organizations, signed a tripartite sectoral policy on HIV prevention in the workplace to fight against HIV-related discrimination.
	 
2. Through a tripartite partnership (Ministry of Social Affairs and Labour, workers&apos; associations and employers&apos; organizations), nearly 305 low-income pregnant women working in the textile sector SONAPI had access to HIV testing. 19, 3311 textile workers (men and women) at SONAPI reduced their vulnerability to HIV and AIDS and to COVID-19 as a result of the training that they received. 1. Through financial and technical support from ILO, for the benefit of the tripartite partners (the Ministry of Social Affairs and Labour, the workers&apos; unions and the employers&apos; unions), a sectoral policy on HIV prevention in the workplace was developed and signed for the textile sector.

2. The ILO provided technical support to constituents in the design and implementation of a VCT@WORK training with a strong component on prevention of HIV and COVID-19. Especially vulnerable workers were targeted, such as low-income pregnant women.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="ES">6.4.1. Number of member States that have measures to ensure equality of opportunities and treatment for persons with disabilities and for at least one of the following groups: indigenous or tribal peoples; ethnic minorities; persons living with HIV; or LGBTI persons</narrative>
    </title>
